<title>UK: FORECAST - Consensus on UK company results.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Consensus on UK company results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of UK company results expected in week ending May 23 include -</p>
<p>COMPANY------------------PFT/DIV/EPS--CONSENSUS----RANGE--------VS</p>
<p>THURSDAY, May 22</p>
<p>Powergen Plc	    **F  PFT	 562.3	528.1-592.0   566.0</p>
<p>				   DIV	  26.3	 25.0-26.3     21.0</p>
<p>				   EPS	  62.6	 59.5-66.5     56.7</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus forecast of PFT 576.5 DIV 25.2 EPS 63.8)</p>
<p>Storehouse Plc	    F  PFT	 119.1	117.5-121.0   109.9</p>
<p>				   DIV	   8.3	  8.2-8.3	 7.2</p>
<p>				   EPS	  19.6	 19.3-19.9     17.8</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus forecast of PFT 120.0 DIV 8.2 EPS 19.6)</p>
<p>Vaux Plc		    H  PFT	  14.6	 14.0-15.0     13.3</p>
<p>				   DIV	   3.7	  3.7-3.9	3.6</p>
<p>All profit figures are pretax, exclude exceptional items unless otherwise stated and are in millions stg. Dividends are total net and quoted as pence per share.</p>
<p>* Previous year's figure is based on proforma as no comparative figures</p>
<p>are available following the Royal Insurance and Sun Alliance merger. ** Figures based on FRS3 accounting definition (i.e. including exceptional</p>
<p>items)</p>
<p>Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 3496</p>
